            "kind": "NO_CODE_CHANGE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "I feel [std::expected](https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/utility/expected.html) is a more idiomatic choice."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "akurdunkar@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "aditya-K2"
                    },
                    "message": "Trying to understand this better. What would be the unexpected type be in the case of std::expected? a `std::error_code`? or maybe an error string? In both cases, really there's just one unexpected state: \"We don't have any instance ids left\". I feel std::optional also conveys the same thing, isn't it?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "There are a couple of error states that need attention. You could probably eliminate `-EINVAL`: https://github.com/openbmc/libpldm/blob/main/include/libpldm/instance-id.h#L53-L69"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 31,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "akurdunkar@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "aditya-K2"
                    },
                    "message": "For this implementation, I think, `-EAGAIN` is the only one that applies. Don't see any other unexpected states that the code could go into. Anyways, the function now returns a `std::error_code` in unexpected states."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is an unexpected program state, log a message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is an illegal program state, right? Log a message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "akurdunkar@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "aditya-K2"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 57,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
                        "email": "akurdunkar@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "aditya-K2"
                    },
                    "message": "Addressed. Logging an error message now."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Andrew Jeffery",
                        "email": "andrew@codeconstruct.com.au",
                        "username": "amboar"
                    },
                    "message": "This is a double-free and a sign of larger problems; log a message?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/InstanceDb.hpp",
                    "line": 58,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Aditya Kurdunkar",
